{"id":"chatcmpl-d1323eac-ae74-48c1-91d5-6c68fe977c3c","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246677,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs. right) about a medical finding in an image. The successful strategy combines a domain-expert query for anatomical reasoning with a grounded localization tool that returns coordinates, then cross-checks the result against explicit image markers (e.g., the 'L' side marker). The key insight is triangulating multiple independent evidence sources before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"For laterality or spatial questions, query a domain expert for anatomical reasoning rather than relying on raw visual inspection alone.\",\n    \"Use a grounded localization tool to obtain coordinates or explicit region labels, then verify them against image-embedded orientation markers.\",\n    \"Cross-check the final answer against at least two independent evidence sources (expert description + grounded report + image marker) before committing.\",\n    \"When options are mutually exclusive binary choices, focus the investigation on the single discriminating attribute (here: which side) rather than describing the whole image.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Ask a domain expert to describe the finding's location using anatomical landmarks, then confirm with a grounded/coordinate-based tool and any orientation markers in the image.\",\n    \"Binary classification with spatial attributes\": \"Identify the one discriminating feature between options and direct all tool calls at resolving that feature, not general description.\",\n    \"Evidence triangulation\": \"Combine expert reasoning, tool-grounded localization, and explicit in-image annotations; agreement across sources justifies the answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image's orientation marker (e.g., 'L'/'R') and map it to patient anatomy before deciding laterality.\",\n    \"Verify that the expert description and the grounded report agree on the same side/region before selecting the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":445,"total_tokens":820,"completion_tokens":375,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":445},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":375}}}